A diagnostic backtrace facility (BOCL:BACKTRACE / %PRINT-BACKTRACE :type :call) made
each blocker fast to localise even though every ASDF load is ~4 min.
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Each blocker below was a *general* CL conformance bug, fixed in the prelude/kernel,
regression-tested (must-* unchanged) and committed+pushed independently:

  - TYPEP: accept '*' bounds in (integer/float/real low high); add (unsigned-byte s),
    (signed-byte s), (mod n), (rational ...) and atomic FUNCTION/BOOLEAN/KEYWORD/
    ATOM/BIT/SIMPLE-*/BASE-CHAR/STANDARD-CHAR.                          (v1.4.10, .12)
       blocked: UIOP (check-type n (integer 0 *)) in source-registry validation, and
       ENSURE-FUNCTION's (etypecase fun (function ...) ((or boolean keyword ...) ...)).
  - PARSE-NAMESTRING added (was exported but undefined).               (v1.4.11)
       blocked: UIOP RESOLVE-ABSOLUTE-LOCATION.
  - CLOS REINITIALIZE-INSTANCE added; SHARED-INITIALIZE fixed so a supplied initarg
    always sets its slot regardless of SLOT-NAMES (CLHS 7.1.3).         (v1.4.13)
       blocked: ASDF RESET-SYSTEM-CLASS ((apply 'reinitialize-instance system keys)).
  - LOOP: ALWAYS/NEVER/THEREIS now tested at their textual position (in the body),
    not before it — so a preceding WHILE/UNTIL or stepped FOR terminates first.  (v1.4.14)
       blocked: (loop for p = parent then (component-parent p) while p
                 thereis (module-default-component-class p)) in PARSE-COMPONENT-FORM.
  - MAKE-PATHNAME: explicit :DIRECTORY NIL stays relative (supplied-p vs DEFAULTS). (v1.4.15)
       blocked: UIOP PARSE-UNIX-NAMESTRING (make-pathname :directory nil :defaults <abs>)
                + ENSURE-PATHNAME :WANT-RELATIVE on each component.
  - CLOS: a method's &KEY lambda list accepts keywords named by sibling methods
    (DEFMETHOD appends &ALLOW-OTHER-KEYS).                              (v1.4.16)
       blocked: OPERATE dispatch passing :VERBOSE to PERFORM methods.
  - WITH-COMPILATION-UNIT macro added (degenerate: PROGN body).         (v1.4.17)
       blocked: ASDF PERFORM plan wraps actions in (with-compilation-unit () ...).
  - CLOS: preserve MULTIPLE VALUES through generic-function dispatch (%CNM-CALL and the
    primary-chain result now use MULTIPLE-VALUE-PROG1).                 (v1.4.18)
       blocked: ASDF COMPONENT-OPERATION-TIME is a (gethash ...) method returning
       (values stamp present-p); the truncated present-p made ACTION-STATUS see done-p
       NIL, so MARK-AS-DONE's stamp/keep-p invariant failed on every system load-op.
       (Also fixed ALREADY-LOADED-SYSTEMS, which now returns ("uiop" "asdf" ...).)

STATUS after v1.4.18: (asdf:defsystem ...) succeeds for all option combinations
(version/description/pathname/components/:depends-on).  (asdf:operate 'load-op "hello")
now gets through find-system, the plan, with-compilation-unit and the stamp/mark-as-done
invariant, and reaches PERFORM.

CURRENT BLOCKER (next): OPERATE re-evaluates the in-progress top-level LOAD form of the
driver file (a nested-LOAD / *load-pathname* / *default-pathname-defaults* re-entrancy),
which under --on-error appease recurses into SIGSEGV.  Tracked separately in
asdf-operate-reenters-toplevel-load.issue — that is the gating bug for actually compiling
