======================================================================
MILESTONE (v1.4.19): USING ASDF — (asdf:load-system "hello") LOADS A REAL
SYSTEM AND RUNS IT.  (asdf:load-system "hello") -> hello:greet returns
"Hello from ASDF on bocl!".
======================================================================
Driven the *proper* way (a .asd on an explicit source-registry, NOT a bare
DEFSYSTEM in the driver):
  (asdf:initialize-source-registry
    '(:source-registry (:directory D) :ignore-inherited-configuration))
  (map () 'asdf:register-immutable-system (asdf:already-loaded-systems))
  (asdf:load-system "hello")   ; find-system -> load-asd -> define-op -> load-op
with D/hello.asd = (defsystem "hello" :components ((:file "pkg")
                                                   (:file "main" :depends-on ("pkg")))).

Three blockers, each diagnosed with the :call-frame backtrace facility:

  1. (RESOLVED — was a TEST-HARNESS ARTIFACT, not a bocl bug) The
     "OPERATE re-evaluates the driver's top-level LOAD form" symptom recorded in
     asdf-operate-reenters-toplevel-load.issue came from calling
     (asdf:defsystem "hello" ...) DIRECTLY in the driver file.  REGISTER-SYSTEM-
     DEFINITION then records the system's source-file as (resolve-symlinks*
     (load-pathname)) = the driver itself, and never marks DEFINE-OP done (only
     LOAD-ASD does, via (setf (component-operation-time define-op sys) t)).  So
     OPERATE planned DEFINE-OP and re-LOADed the driver.  The conforming flow —
     a .asd found through the source-registry and loaded by LOAD-ASD — does not
     hit this: hello's source-file is hello.asd and DEFINE-OP is already done.
     => issue closed (moved to issues/closed/).

  2. MAKE-PATHNAME did not inherit NAME/TYPE from :DEFAULTS (only DIRECTORY/DEVICE).
     So (make-pathname :type "fasl" :defaults #P".../pkg.lisp") -> #P".../.fasl"
     (name dropped), and ASDF's OUTPUT-FILES :around (ensure-absolute-pathname +
     *output-translation-function*) collapsed it to the bare directory.  LOAD-OP
     then tried to LOAD that directory -> getc() EISDIR -> STREAM-ERROR.
     FIX (prelude): make-pathname now fills unsupplied NAME/TYPE from DEFAULTS
     (supplied-p flags, so an explicit :NAME NIL — the directory-pathname idiom —
     still strips the file part).  CLHS-conformant and general.            (v1.4.19)

  3. FILE-WRITE-DATE signalled a generic SIMPLE-ERROR for a missing file; UIOP's
     SAFE-FILE-WRITE-DATE does (handler-case (file-write-date p) (file-error () nil))
     while planning (generated outputs — the fasls bocl never writes — don't exist
     yet), so the error escaped and aborted planning.
     FIX (prelude): file-write-date now signals FILE-ERROR (CLHS) for a missing
     file (wraps the kernel primitive; probe-file first).                  (v1.4.19)

  4. Interpreter compile/load model: bocl writes no fast-load file, so UIOP's
     COMPILE-FILE* temp-file -> rename -> load-the-fasl machinery is meaningless
     (it opens a temp with :ELEMENT-TYPE :DEFAULT — which bocl rejects — and would
     then rename a non-existent fasl).  FIX (asdf.lisp #+bocl): override PERFORM so
     COMPILE-OP on a CL-SOURCE-FILE is a no-op and LOAD-OP loads the component's
     SOURCE directly via CL:LOAD (bocl interprets the forms in order — IN-PACKAGE /
     DEFMACRO / EVAL-WHEN honoured — which is exactly what loading the would-be
     fasl achieves).  This bypasses COMPILE-FILE* entirely.               (v1.4.19)

NON-BLOCKING, filed while here (in index):
  - open-element-type-default.issue — OPEN/WITH-OPEN-FILE reject :ELEMENT-TYPE
    :DEFAULT (convert_element_type in kernel.c).  No longer on the ASDF path after
    blocker #4, but any WITH-TEMPORARY-FILE user hits it.

USING-ASDF leg is COMPLETE.  Remaining work in this (large, multi-tier) issue is the
broader UIOP surface — Tier-2 RUN-PROGRAM / real COMPILE-FILE* condition capture,
Tier-3 launch-program — exercised only by systems whose build ops need subprocesses.

== STATE RE-ASSESSMENT (v1.5.7) ==
Checked the implementation before processing (index rule).  Much of TIER 1 is now
already in place:
- *FEATURES* has :BOCL :UNIX :LINUX :X86-64 (item 1 DONE).
- bocl:getenv / bocl:getcwd / bocl:chdir present (item 2 DONE); bocl command-line
  arguments accessor present (item 3 DONE).
- CL:DIRECTORY enumerates wildcards (e.g. "/tmp/*" -> 158 entries) via the
  %DIRECTORY-GLOB kernel primitive (item 4 DONE for the wildcard path).
- CONDITION HIERARCHY (item 5, the stated first-error blocker) is RESOLVED:
  (typep (make-condition 'style-warning) 'warning) => T and
  (subtypep 'style-warning 'warning) => (T T).  See clos-condition-hierarchy-parents.

REMAINING (this stays an open epic — the real deliverable is ASDF loading and
OPERATE-ing end to end, which is iterative and touches many subsystems):
- TIER 2 item 6: bocl:run-program / bocl:%system (fork+exec+waitpid) is NOT yet
  implemented (find-symbol RUN-PROGRAM/%SYSTEM in BOCL => NIL).  ASDF core does not
  need it, but build ops do.
- TIER 2 item 7: verify UIOP COMPILE-FILE* condition capture against bocl's
  COMPILE-FILE multiple-value return.
- TIER 3: launch-program / async spawn (optional, UIOP tolerates
  NOT-IMPLEMENTED-ERROR).
- End-to-end: walk the ASDF load to completion and add the remaining #+bocl
  branches as each NOT-IMPLEMENTED-ERROR / gap is hit.
Not put on hold for a dependency (the condition blocker is cleared) — kept open as
an epic advanced incrementally as ASDF is driven.
